From 47c8693b0c5393b0bc317f6e9750ccaa6b66df54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Curd Becker <me@curd-becker.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] input: factor HID keyboard report handling out of
 apple_spi_kbd

Turning a boot-keyboard-style report (modifier bits for usages E0-E7 and
an array of Keyboard/Keypad usages) into key events is not specific to
the Apple SPI keyboard. Move the usage table and the old/new report
comparison into hid_kbd.c (CONFIG_HID_KBD, selected by the drivers that
use it), so that other HID keyboard drivers share them instead of
carrying their own copies.

No functional change: the table is unchanged, and the events are the
same and in the same order (modifiers in the driver's order, then per
key slot the released key before the pressed one).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
